      "code_path": "src/Nethermind/Nethermind.TxPool/Filters/MalformedTxFilter.cs::Accept::L21-22",
      "proof_trace": "TxPool and BlockValidator share the same TxValidator singleton that enforces Eip7825Constants.DefaultTxGasLimitCap (16,777,216). However, TxPool uses GetCurrentHeadSpec() while BlockValidator uses GetSpec(block.Header), creating a race window during fork activation where TxPool may accept transactions under the old spec that BlockValidator rejects under the new spec.",
      "attack_scenario": "During EIP-7825 fork activation at block N, submit transaction with gasLimit=20M. TxPool accepts it (old spec, cap=MaxValue), peers broadcast it, but block producers reject it when building block N (new spec, cap=16,777,216). This creates mempool pollution and wastes network bandwidth on un-mineable transactions.",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-aa9e39fd-inv-008"
    }
  ]
}

